  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Logan Webb lasted three innings at Coors Field and the game was over by the time anyone realized it started.",
    "what_this_means": "Colorado scored seven runs in the fifth. The Giants never led and never recovered. This is what a blowout looks like from the inside. No drama, no late push, just 12 runs down and daylight between every inning. Webb got touched for seven hits and seven earned runs in a short outing. The bullpen tried to limit damage after that, but the game had already broken. The lineup managed eight hits and ten strikeouts, converted runners on base twice, but nothing mounted. One run in the third, one in the fourth, and then nothing. Coors Field amplified every mistake Webb made early. This team can't afford to spot anyone four runs before the second inning ends and still expect to win.",
    "what_to_watch": "Robbie Ray takes the mound tonight against Tomoyuki Sugano, who's carrying a 4.80 ERA into the series. Ray has a 1.72 ERA over his last four starts. The one clear thing working right now.",
